Generation from an acquired orthogonal line
==========================================

This is a sufficient criterion for the existing F004 intake. It introduces
no classification theorem and gives no result for any current case until
its hypotheses and numerical certificates have been acquired. All code in
this operational Source packet was unexecuted at authoring.

Hypotheses
----------

Let V be the acquired faithful seven-dimensional natural module of
G=G2(11). Its nondegenerate symmetric bilinear form is denoted B. The
particular original frame, the identification with G, the four original
marks a,b,c,e in G, and the complete catalogue/orbit/member/transporter
meaning are imported separately. An abstract group name or an arbitrary
faithful seven-dimensional representation is insufficient.

Suppose the four marks are distinct nonidentity involutions and satisfy
the distant commutations for the ordered quartet. In particular a,e
commute. The acquired common positive eigenspace of a,e is one-dimensional,
spanned by the actual stored seed v, and B(v,v) is nonzero. Every mark is
an isometry of this same B. Put H=<a,b,c,e>.

The endpoint projector
----------------------

Since the characteristic is odd, an involutory isometry is self-adjoint.
Consequently the commuting product p=(I+a)(I+e)/4 is self-adjoint and
idempotent, with image the common positive eigenspace. Its image is the
nonsingular line spanned by v. Therefore

  x*p = B(x,v)*v/B(v,v).

The operational checker verifies this complete matrix equation, using the
acquired actual seed and the pure seven-dimensional block of the same
normalization form. It checks the actual nonzero seed norm as well. Thus
it does not replace this particular projector by an arbitrary cyclic line.
The isometry/nondegeneracy and complete original model joins remain
explicit Root-owned premises; the matrix equation is not a new model
recognition algorithm. Since p=(I+a)(I+e)/4, p belongs to F11[H].

From orbit rows to the full matrix algebra
------------------------------------------

Supply seven original rows w0,...,w6, with w0=v. Each later row has an
earlier parent and a label of one of the four original marks, and its full
row equation is checked. Induction gives wi=v*hi for a genuine word hi
in H. Supply a right inverse R of the full row matrix A and check A*R=I7.
The seven rows then form a basis of V.

For right actions and every i,j,

  x*(hi^-1*p*hj)=B(x*hi^-1,v)*wj/B(v,v)
                =B(x,wi)*wj/B(v,v).

The second equality uses that hi is an isometry. Nondegeneracy and the
basis property imply that the seven functionals B(-,wi)/B(v,v) form a
basis of V*. The displayed49 operators consequently form a basis of
End(V). Each belongs to F11[H], so F11[H]=End(V), and H is irreducible.
These49 operators are algebra elements, not necessarily matrix units or
group elements. They are never supplied to a word evaluator as group
words. Only the genuine parent-tree words hi are used by discovery.

An arbitrary cyclic vector would not suffice: the companion module
F11[X]/((X-1)f6(X)), for an irreducible degree-six polynomial f6, is
cyclic and reducible. The endpoint projector is the essential extra leg.

The prime-order witness
-----------------------

Supply a genuine quartet word W of length at most32 using all four
labels. Check its actual matrix, Y=W^6, Y!=I7 and Y^37=I7, including
every entry of the supplied Y. Prime37 then gives exact order37 in H.
The complete retained natural G2(11) maximal-overgroup theorem states
that every proper subgroup containing37 is contained in a maximal
SU3(11):2. In this natural embedding that maximal subgroup stabilizes
a nonisotropic rational line. Such an H is reducible, contradicting the
preceding conclusion. Thus H=G.

The cofactor6 is only a sufficient search choice; no assertion that it
always succeeds is used. A finite search miss, a lower-rank cyclic
acquisition or an interrupted case supplies no nongeneration certificate.
GEN itself supplies neither the rank-four intersection property nor a
settled case. End properties, mutual end intersection, standard gluing
and any final disposition remain separate duties.

Acquisition and verification
-----------------------------

Discovery starts at v and stores unreduced actual orbit rows. A separate
echelon workspace decides independence; a reduced combination is never
stored as an orbit row. Each stored row is processed under four marks,
and an independent image records its earlier parent and label. At most
seven independent rows and28 candidate images occur. A queue that closes
below rank7 is inconclusive in this packet. At rank7, Gauss-Jordan on a
copy of the original A proposes R, and the full product A*R is checked.

The separate direct entry never calls acquisition, row reduction or
candidate search. It checks every supplied original identity, all six
parent edges, the full inverse, the endpoint-projector equation and any
positive prime-order word. Thus discovery's elimination is outside the
trusted numerical certificate argument.

